<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kulottunga I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1070–<a href="/years/1122">1122</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Kulothunga Chola I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kulottunga I was emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola Empire</a> from 1070 to 1122. Born Rajendra, son of the Eastern Chalukya king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajaraja-narendra">Rajaraja Narendra</a> and a Chola princess, he united the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vengi">Vengi</a> kingdom with the Chola realm on taking the Chola throne. His long reign was a time of stability, and he is remembered for abolishing tolls and for diplomatic relations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kulottunga-i.jpg" alt="Kulottunga I" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matthew T Rader · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sculpture_in_a_wall_at_Nataraja_Temple_in_Chidambaram,_Tamil_Nadu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
